      "message": "(1) In ag/15974921,  for the system API of WifiManager#addCustomDhcpOption(),  we use DhcpOption as a parameter.  There is a build failure on the target of aosp_bramble-userdebug on git_master branch (a CheckBuild).   The build error message is: \n\npackages/modules/Wifi/framework/java/android/net/wifi/WifiManager.java:9152: error: Class android.net.DhcpOption is hidden but was referenced (as parameter type) from public parameter options in android.net.wifi.WifiManager.addCustomDhcpOptions(android.net.wifi.WifiSsid ssid, byte[] oui, java.util.List\u003candroid.net.DhcpOption\u003e options) [ReferencesHidden]Error: metalava detected the following problems:\npackages/modules/Wifi/framework/java/android/net/wifi/WifiManager.java:9152: error: Class android.net.DhcpOption is hidden but was referenced (as parameter type) from public parameter options in android.net.wifi.WifiManager.addCustomDhcpOptions(android.net.wifi.WifiSsid ssid, byte[] oui, java.util.List\u003candroid.net.DhcpOption\u003e options) [ReferencesHidden]\n\nAfter it is changed to client.privilegedapps,  the build is successful.  (Thanks Nate for helping to figure this out.)\n\n\n2. Samsung app / OEM framework will call WifiManager#addCustomDhcpOption() to set their custom DhcpOption options.  I think this can be viewed a privileged app model.",
